VTID-03787 — commands.log
==========================

## Why this VTID exists

VTID-03785 and VTID-03786 (both merged, both deployed to staging, both
mutation-tested) removed every known instance of two "risky phrase"
pattern classes from the guided-topic system-instruction path across all
3 injection points found (guided-topic-narration-prompt.ts,
live-session-controller.ts's buildVertexWakeBriefBlock, orb-livekit.ts's
firstTurnSuppressionDirective — the last two found via a Codex P1 review
finding, verified against the code before fixing).

Live re-test after VTID-03786 deployed (6 real sessions, 6 different
topics, via the raw-TLS-over-proxy-tunnel SSE harness against real
staging):

  T001, T002, T003, T004, T005, T251: 6/6 BLOCKED

Cross-checked via oasis_events — all 12 events (6 sessions x 2 attempts
each) identical:
  code: nova_validation
  diagnostic: "This request has been blocked by our content filters."

Also ruled out tool declarations as the differentiator: `novaTools` is
derived from the same `buildLiveApiTools()` output used for every
authenticated session (guided or not) — confirmed by reading orb-live.ts
directly (novaTools <- setup.tools <- buildLiveApiTools(...), same call
site both session types share).

Conclusion: the "risky phrase" theory is falsified as the sole cause.
Rather than guess a 4th pattern, get real data.

