## Follow-up (Codex P1 finding, addressed before merge)

Codex review on PR #3226 flagged: the new `nova_instruction_debug_dump`
diag row carries the full literal Nova instruction text (real user memory/
personalization context) but, like every orb.live.diag stage, never sets
metadata.tenant_id. tenant-admin/overview.ts's GET /activity endpoint
treats any oasis_events row with no tenant_id as "global" and includes it
for every tenant admin — so this stage's raw payload could reach a tenant
admin who isn't the session's own user.

Verified directly against the code before acting (not blindly trusted):
  - Read tenant-admin/overview.ts:171-186 — confirmed the exact filter
    `meta.tenant_id === tenantId || !meta.tenant_id` (no tenant_id ->
    included for everyone).
  - Read emitDiag() (orb-live.ts:15000) — confirmed NO orb.live.diag stage
    ever sets tenant_id; this is a pre-existing, repo-wide pattern, not
    something unique to this PR. But every other diag stage carries only
    booleans/counts/reasons — this is the first to carry raw literal user
    context, which is what makes the gap actually dangerous here.
  - Checked GET /alerts (overview.ts:193-217): filters status IN
    (error,critical); emitLiveSessionEvent defaults status to 'info' for
    diag events (orb-live.ts:14974) — confirmed /alerts is NOT a leak path
    for this stage.

Fix: tenant-admin/overview.ts's GET /activity now excludes any oasis_events
row whose metadata.stage is in a new SENSITIVE_DIAG_STAGES set (currently
just 'nova_instruction_debug_dump'), BEFORE the tenant_id check — closes
the leak regardless of whether tenant_id is ever set on the emitting side.

New test: "GET /activity excludes nova_instruction_debug_dump diag rows
even without a tenant_id (VTID-03787)".

$ npx jest test/routes/tenant-admin/overview.test.ts
PASS — 15/15 (was 14/14 before this fix)

Mutation-verified: removed the SENSITIVE_DIAG_STAGES check, re-ran —
new test fails exactly as expected (e2 leaks into tenant admin's
activity feed), confirming the test pins real behavior. Restored,
re-ran clean.

